{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[2\\sin(-4x-3)\\right]$ is the *second derivative* of $2\\sin(-4x-3)$. In other words, it's the derivative of $\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[2\\sin(-4x-3)\\right]$, which is the derivative of $2\\sin(-4x-3)$.\n\nBecause of this, we need to differentiate $2\\sin(-4x-3)$ twice in order to find $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[2\\sin(-4x-3)\\right]$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's start by finding $\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[2\\sin(-4x-3)\\right]$:\n\n$\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[2\\sin(-4x-3)\\right]=-8\\cos(-4x-3)$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[2\\sin(-4x-3)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=2\\cos(-4x-3)\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}(-4x-3)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=2\\cos(-4x-3)\\cdot(-4)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-8\\cos(-4x-3)\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"Now we can differentiate $-8\\cos(-4x-3)$ to find $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[2\\sin(-4x-3)\\right]$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[2\\sin(-4x-3)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-8\\cos(-4x-3)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-32\\sin(-4x-3)\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[2\\sin(-4x-3)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-8\\cos(-4x-3)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-8\\left[-\\sin(-4x-3)\\right]\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}(-4x-3)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=8\\sin(-4x-3)\\cdot(-4)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-32\\sin(-4x-3)\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[2\\sin(-4x-3)\\right]=-32\\sin(-4x-3)$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Find $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[2\\sin(-4x-3)\\right]$.**\n\n[[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"-32\\sin(-4x-3)"}],"buttonSets":["basic","trig","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
